    <md:title>4.10.4: Comparing Graphs and Statements that Represent Functions without a Context</md:title>
    <md:uuid>335e9f8b-81c8-4d14-a910-76704f01a0f9</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Here are graphs that represent two <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">functions</term>, \(f\) and \(g\).</para>
<para><figure><media alt="A graph. "><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/176b15619517ba5f9c3a25499139e7048af8b04b"/></media></figure></para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
      <para>Decide which function value is greater for each given input. Be prepared to explain your reasoning.
        </para><para>Which is greater, \(f(2)\) or \(g(2)\)</para>
        </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(g(2)\) is greater.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Which is greater, \(f(4)\) or \(g(4)\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>They appear to be equal.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
      <para>Which is greater, \(f(6)\) or \(g(6)\)</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(f(6)\) is greater.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
      <para>Which is greater, \(f(8)\) or \(g(8)\)</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(f(8)\) is greater.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Is there a value of \(x\) at which the <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip"> equation</term> \(f(x)=g(x)\) is true? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    <para>Yes. For example: If the graphs intersect when \(x\) is 4 and when it is 9, then \(f(4)=g(4)\) and \(f(9)=g(9)\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Identify at least two values of \(x\) at which the inequality \(f(x)&lt;g(x)\) is true.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    <para>1, 3, 10, 11, or other \(x\)-values that are less than 4 and greater than 9</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
